{"id":"91a7","full_id":"restart-matrix-91a7","name":"autonomous:decompose","task":"You are decomposing a feature request into a structured Product Requirements Document.\n\nSCOPE (hard boundary):\n- Project directory: /home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/project\n- You may WRITE only under: /home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/project\n- Do not read, write or list anything outside these directories.\n- All output files, notes and checkpoints go under the project directory, using paths relative to it.\n\nThe project directory above is the ONLY place this work happens. Every task you\nwrite must be doable inside the directories above; never tell a worker to work in\nanother repository or directory, and use paths relative to the project directory.\nIf the feature request names another repository or URL, treat it as a subject to\nresearch (web or read-only), not as a place to work.\n\nBefore writing the plan, explore the project to understand what already exists —\nread files that are relevant to the feature request (source code, config, docs,\nor whatever the spec calls for).\n\nIMPORTANT: follow the feature request faithfully.\n- If the spec asks for research, research.\n- If the spec asks for implementation, explore source code.\n- Do NOT use prior planning documents, historical PRD outputs, or other\n  decomposition artifacts as a substitute for what the spec asks for. Those are\n  records of past work, not instructions for this task.\n- Base the decomposition on the feature request below and what you observe in\n  the project — not on what previous plans happened to produce.\n\nAfter exploring, write the decomposition as raw JSON to this file:\n/home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/project/.decompose-output-08e76eb3af1bd947.json\n\nThe JSON must follow this schema exactly:\n{\n  \"title\": \"\u003cshort feature title\u003e\",\n  \"stories\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\u003cstory title\u003e\",\n      \"description\": \"\u003cone-paragraph description\u003e\",\n      \"files\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"verification_script\": \"\u003crepo-relative path to an executable verification script you wrote, or empty string — see the Verification scripts section below\u003e\",\n      \"files_generated\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"\u003ctask title\u003e\",\n          \"spec\": \"\u003cconcrete instructions for one worker session — include file paths and context from your exploration\u003e\",\n          \"files\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [],\n          \"verification_script\": \"\u003crepo-relative path to an executable verification script you wrote, or empty string — see the Verification scripts section below\u003e\",\n          \"files_generated\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n          \"kind\": \"\u003csmoke|final_gate\u003e\" // optional — \"smoke\" for a live smoke-test task, \"final_gate\" for the end-to-end verification task\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- depends_on lists either story or task titles that must complete first.\n- Each task spec must be self-contained — the worker won't see other tasks.\n- Aim for 1-3 stories per PRD, 1-5 tasks per story. Prefer fewer, well-scoped tasks.\n- \"kind\" (optional): tag a task that is a live smoke test with \"smoke\",\n  and the task that verifies the whole feature end-to-end as a final gate\n  with \"final_gate\". Ordinary tasks should omit the field (or use \"\").\n- verification_script / files_generated (B124/BL416): these two fields are\n  part of this schema, not optional extras — fill them in per any\n  \"Verification scripts\" instructions appended below. An empty string for\n  verification_script is only correct for a unit with no applicable\n  check (e.g. a pure-research story producing no files); every unit that\n  touches real files should have one.\n- Verification scripts must check only the files their unit of work\n  changes (e.g. list them from 'git diff --name-only' plus the untracked\n  files, or name them explicitly) and must never run gofmt or a similar\n  formatter over a whole package or directory — unrelated files that\n  were already unformatted would fail the task.\n- Never write a literal absolute path to a system binary (e.g. /usr/bin/foo\n  or /bin/bar) in a task spec. Refer to standard system tools by command\n  name only (e.g. \"the time command\") and have the task resolve them at\n  runtime via \"command -v \u003cname\u003e\" / $PATH, with a graceful fallback if\n  unavailable. Any literal absolute path in a spec must be one the task\n  will actually read or write under the directories above.\n- Release tasks never contain a fixed version number. The release version is\n  taken at merge time as the next patch above main; write 'next patch above\n  main' in task titles, specs and descriptions instead of a number, and do not\n  repeat a number even if a revision note or earlier plan used one.\n- Write ONLY raw JSON to the file — no markdown fences, no explanatory prose.\n\nFeature request:\nYou are planning a feature request into a structured Product Requirements Document with stories and tasks.\n\nReturn ONLY a JSON object with this shape:\n{\n  \"title\": \"\u003cshort feature title\u003e\",\n  \"stories\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\u003cstory title\u003e\",\n      \"description\": \"\u003cone-paragraph description\u003e\",\n      \"files\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n      \"depends_on\": [],\n      \"tasks\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"\u003ctask title\u003e\",\n          \"spec\": \"\u003cconcrete instructions for one worker session\u003e\",\n          \"files\": [\"\u003crepo-relative path\u003e\", \"...\"],\n          \"depends_on\": [],\n          \"kind\": \"\u003csmoke|final_gate\u003e\" // optional, see the kind rule below\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nRules:\n- depends_on lists either story or task titles that must complete first.\n- Each task's spec must be self-contained — the worker won't see other tasks.\n- Aim for 1-3 stories per PRD, 1-5 tasks per story. Prefer fewer, well-scoped tasks.\n- \"kind\" (optional): tag a task that is a live smoke test with \"smoke\",\n  and the task that verifies the whole feature end-to-end as a final gate\n  with \"final_gate\". Ordinary tasks should omit the field (or use \"\").\n- \"files\" (Phase 4, v5.26.67): list repo-relative paths each story or\n  task is expected to touch. Include both code and docs/test files.\n  Empty array is valid when paths are unknown ahead of time. Do NOT\n  invent paths that obviously can't exist.\n- Verification scripts must check only the files their unit of work\n  changes (e.g. list them from 'git diff --name-only' plus the untracked\n  files, or name them explicitly) and must never run gofmt or a similar\n  formatter over a whole package or directory — unrelated files that\n  were already unformatted would fail the task.\n- Never write a literal absolute path to a system binary (e.g. /usr/bin/foo\n  or /bin/bar) in a task spec. Refer to standard system tools by command\n  name only (e.g. \"the time command\") and have the task resolve them at\n  runtime via \"command -v \u003cname\u003e\" / $PATH, with a graceful fallback if\n  unavailable. Any literal absolute path in a spec must be one the task\n  will actually read or write under the PRD's allowed directories.\n- Release tasks never contain a fixed version number. The release version is\n  taken at merge time as the next patch above main; write 'next patch above\n  main' in task titles, specs and descriptions instead of a number, and do not\n  repeat a number even if a revision note or earlier plan used one.\n- Do not include markdown fences. Return raw JSON only.\n\nFeature request:\nRestart matrix probe: write a result file.\n\n\n--- Verification scripts ---\nBefore finalizing your JSON plan, give each task (or story, when a story-level check fits that unit of work better) whose verification this project's rules require a real verification script:\n1. Reuse first. Run a real `ls scripts/` and `head`/`grep` the candidates — do not trust a hand-copied list of scripts, it drifts; check what's already there. Also check AGENT.md and CONTEXT.md for commands that already cover what the unit needs to verify, before writing anything new.\n2. Write an executable script at `.datawatch/verify/\u003cname\u003e.sh` (relative to your working directory) running whatever this repo's rules require for the files that unit touches. Work out what applies to THIS repo — no specific tool is assumed. IDs are assigned only after your plan is parsed, so \u003cname\u003e is a short, unique, filesystem-safe slug of the task (or story) title. `chmod +x` it.\n3. In the JSON, set that unit's `verification_script` to the relative path and also list the same path in its `files_generated` array.\n4. A script must check only the files its task changes — for example by listing them from `git diff --name-only` plus the untracked files, or by naming them explicitly — and must never run gofmt or a similar formatter over a whole package or directory, because unrelated files that were already unformatted would fail the task.\n5. If neither AGENT.md nor CONTEXT.md exists, do not skip verification: detect the ecosystem conventions actually present (Makefile lint/test targets, package.json scripts, pyproject.toml, go.mod + standard go tooling, etc.) and script from those.\nDo NOT inline any file content (scripts, rules files, source) in your response — only the verification_script path goes in the JSON; write script bodies to disk with your own tools.\n","project_dir":"/home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/project","tmux_session":"cs-restart-matrix-91a7","log_file":"/home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/data/sessions/restart-matrix-91a7/output.log","state":"killed","created_at":"2026-10-24T04:31:20.860988928-04:00","updated_at":"2026-10-24T04:31:24.03701631-04:00","hostname":"restart-matrix","group_id":"","backend_family":"shell","llm_ref":"shell","tracking_dir":"/home/dmz/.datawatch/prd-worktrees/d0210001/.rm-work/rm.b5xThG/git-operation/data/sessions/restart-matrix-91a7","console_cols":80,"console_rows":24,"output_mode":"terminal","input_mode":"tmux","summary_generated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","effort":"normal","scrub_tmux_env":true,"last_channel_event_at":"2026-10-24T04:31:21.121602919-04:00","one_shot":true,"prd_id":"619f0001","skip_snapshot":true}